.TH "acwm-portal" "1" "2026-11-17" "acwm-portal @VERSION@" "acwm-portal manual"

.SH NAME
acwm-portal \- screenshot portal backend for acwm

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBacwm-portal\fP [\fB\-h\fP | \fB\-\-help\fP]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBacwm-portal\fP is a standalone session-bus service that implements
.B org.freedesktop.impl.portal.Screenshot
(see \fBxdg-desktop-portal\fP(1)). It is meant to be started by D-Bus
activation and registers the bus name
.B org.freedesktop.impl.portal.desktop.acwm
so \fBxdg-desktop-portal\fP can route screenshot requests from sandboxed or
portal-using applications to it.

Captures are performed directly from the running acwm compositor through the
\fBzwlr_screencopy_v1\fP protocol. The captured output is the one under the
pointer, resolved via acwm's IPC socket; the PNG is written to a private file
under
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/acwm-portal/
and returned to the portal front-end as a \fBfile://\fR URI.

This backend is non-interactive: requests are answered immediately without
showing a chooser.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Wayland display used to connect to acwm.
.TP
.B ACWM_PORTAL_OUTPUT
Output name to capture instead of the one under the pointer.
.TP
.B ACWM_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE
Path of the acwm IPC socket, used to locate the pointer. Set by acwm on
startup.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR acwm (1),
.BR xdg-desktop-portal (1)
